  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\sqrt{2xy-1})) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\sqrt{2xy-1}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(2xy-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum and the constant multiple rules for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(2xy-1) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}(2x\\cdot \\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(y)-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot (2x\\cdot 1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
